    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions of the street.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along the access drive that may reduce vertical or side clearance for emergency vehicles.\n• Mark the rear access point with a clearly visible sign or reflective indicator so responders can locate it quickly.\n• Keep the rear access gate unlocked or secured with a breakaway latch to allow emergency entry without delay.\n• Clear dense vegetation away from the sides of the access drive to allow vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Trim shrubs and low branches near the front entry area so responders can move freely on foot between the parking area and the entrance.\n• Keep the walkway between the front entry and parking area clear of parked vehicles, equipment, or stored items.\n• Mark any gate or fence opening that provides access to the detached structure so responders can identify it without searching.\n• Thin dense vegetation between the main residence and the detached structure to allow responders to move between the two buildings.\n• Post a simple site map near the driveway entrance showing the location of the main residence, detached structure, and any access gates."
