    "recommendations": "• Thin trees in the cluster nearest to the structure to create more open space between the trees and the building.\n• Trim shrubs that are growing directly next to or touching the structure.\n• Cut back brush in the brush area closest to the structure to reduce the amount of burnable material nearby.\n• Mow or cut grass cover around the structure and near any outbuildings to keep it short and reduce ground-level burning.\n• Remove low-hanging branches from scattered trees near the structure so fire cannot climb from the ground into the tree canopy.\n• Keep vegetation along all driveway and access routes trimmed back so vehicles can pass freely and visibility is clear in both directions.\n• Separate any shrubs or small trees that are touching or nearly touching each other in the area between the brush zone and the structure."
